AB  - Modern software requires efficient and reliable automated test case generation, whereas manual testing often suffers from being time-consuming and inconsistent. This paper proposes a Quality-Guarded-Behavior Driven Development for automated test case generation. The proposed model integrates an Attention-DistilBERT-Support Vector Machine, where DistilBERT is utilized to capture contextual embeddings, a word vector attention mechanism emphasizes important tokens, and the Support Vector Machine provides robust requirement classification. This integration of testability-aware pipeline detects contextual anomalies during training and employs a runtime self-healing Behavior Driven Development mechanism using fuzzy matching. The anomaly-aware learning mechanism reduces the influence of unclear or ambiguous requirements. The experimental results show that the proposed model achieved a high accuracy of 98.7%, improving the quality of downstream Behavior Driven Development based test case generation. As a result, the framework enhances understanding of requirements, reduces ambiguity, and produces high-quality test cases.
ER  - 

