AB  - Flaky tests are tests that pass or fail non-deterministically. They may succeed in one run and fail in another without any change in the code. Such behavior reduces developer confidence in the test suite. It also increases CI/CD pipeline time because engineers often rerun builds to confirm failures. In addition, flaky tests make it difficult to detect real regressions. This paper presents ATRA (Advanced Test Report Analyzer), a framework designed to analyze and visualize historical Cucumber BDD test results. The framework automatically collects test results from multiple historical runs stored in a Git repository. It then processes and classifies each test scenario based on its behavior across runs. ATRA categorizes scenarios into four classes: Consistently Failing, Flaky, New Failure, and Consistently Passing. This classification helps Quality Engineers (QEs) quickly understand the health of the test suite. The framework provides an interactive interface where QEs can select a time window of historical runs for analysis. ATRA then generates comparative reports that include trend line graphs and status distribution pie charts. These visualizations help engineers identify unstable tests and observe failure trends over time. In addition, ATRA allows QEs to record investigation notes directly within the framework. These notes are automatically committed back to the Git repository, creating a traceable history of test analysis and debugging activities.
ER  - 

