AB  - Effective software testing plays a key role in ensuring the quality of developed systems. Behavior-Driven Development (BDD) is an approach that promotes collaboration between technical and non-technical team members through a language based on describing the expected behavior of the system. In this research, we explore the possibilities of automated BDD scenario generation from use cases, aiming to reduce manual effort and eliminate ambiguities between teams. We compare three approaches: a manual method using NLP libraries, generation using language models with a zero-shot approach, and an extended approach using a few-shot method supported by text analysis tools. The results show that a combination of artificial intelligence, rules, and example cases provides the highest quality, consistency, and practical usability of test scenarios. The proposed solution can contribute to improving test automation in the early stages of development and support communication between technical teams and stakeholders.
ER  - 

